# UNINTENTIONAL FLIGHT INTO ICING (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist booklet, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05, page 23 (owner decisions 2026-10-23, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28: the booklet is binding): the heading line "Leave icing area, inform ATC, continue with item 1" as a comment line, the checklist INADVERTENT ICING ENCOUNTER & EXCESSIVE ICE ACCUMULATION with its ten numbered rows and the * markers, the footnote and the follow-on checklist ICE PROTECTION FAILURE with its six rows and the table, every text as printed. The row marks are the numbers as the booklet counts them (1 to 10, then 1 to 6 for the follow-on checklist, which restarts after its title line, lint L16). Graded are rows 1 to 8 and 10; the follow-on checklist and the table are display rows (not graded in this situation). Row 1: Ice-protection system HI + MAX is graded on the DE-ICE MODE toggle at HIGH; the MAX press is a momentary button that leaves no state behind, so it is not graded. Row 2 is the PROP DE-ICE switch ON (no effect yet, the state is graded); row 4 is the ICE LIGHT position of the ice-light toggle, optional as printed "as required" (its effect stays open); row 5 Cabin heat ON is TEMPERATURE at 75 or WARM, the same rule as the warm air that melts the ice; row 6 Cabin air DEFROST is DIRECTION at DEFROST; row 7 is an increase of the POWER lever; row 8 is ALTERNATE AIR open; row 9 Windshield de-ice USE AS APPROPRIATE is the WIND SHIELD press, a momentary button, so it is a display row (the spray and its protection run in the physics); row 10 is the emergency window, optional as printed "as required". The booklet has no alternate static row. All other text is own wording. The ice growth, the length of the icing area, the onset window and the cue bound are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: icing-unintentional
title: ICING CONDITIONS
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: "Page 23, UNINTENTIONAL FLIGHT INTO ICING"
  verified: "2026-10-28"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cloud
briefing:
  situation: "You are flying in cloud when ice begins to form on the windscreen. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The ice builds up on both halves of the windscreen, and the ice protection, the pitot heating, the cabin heat and the alternate air source are not in use."
initial:
  controls:
    sw.deice_mode: "off"
    sw.prop_deice: "off"
    sw.pitot_stall_heat: "off"
    lv.env_temp: cold
    lv.env_direction: face
    lv.alt_air: closed
  quantities:
    ice_pilot: 15
    ice_copilot: 15
parameters:
  ice_accretion: 0.5
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: UNINTENTIONAL FLIGHT INTO ICING
procedure[24]:
  - kind: comment
    text: "Leave icing area, inform ATC, continue with item 1"
  - kind: comment
    text: "* INADVERTENT ICING ENCOUNTER & * EXCESSIVE ICE ACCUMULATION"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_deice
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: deice_high
        severity: critical
        number: 1
        text: "* Ice-protection system"
        action: "HI + MAX"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.deice_mode
          is: high
  - kind: group
    id: grp_prop_deice
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: prop_deice_on
        severity: critical
        number: 2
        text: "* Prop De-Ice"
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.prop_deice
          is: "on"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_pitot
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: pitot_heat_on
        severity: critical
        number: 3
        text: "Pitot/Stall heat"
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.pitot_stall_heat
          is: "on"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ice_light
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ice_light_on
        severity: optional
        number: 4
        text: "* Ice light"
        action: "ON as required"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.deice_ice_light
          is: ice_light
  - kind: group
    id: grp_cabin_heat
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: cabin_heat_on
        severity: critical
        number: 5
        text: "ECS - Cabin heat"
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state_in
          control: lv.env_temp
          in[2]: t75,warm
  - kind: group
    id: grp_cabin_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: cabin_air_defrost
        severity: critical
        number: 6
        text: "ECS - Cabin air"
        action: "DEFROST"
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.env_direction
          is: defrost
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_increase
        severity: standard
        number: 7
        text: "Power lever"
        action: "INCREASE, change periodically"
        done:
          check: travel_rel
          control: lv.power
          op: gt
          delta: 0
  - kind: group
    id: grp_alt_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt_air_open
        severity: critical
        number: 8
        text: "Alternate air"
        action: "OPEN"
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.alt_air
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: 9
    text: "* Windshield de-ice"
    action: "USE AS APPROPRIATE"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: 10
        text: "Emergency front windows"
        action: "OPEN as required"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: "* If ice-protection does not work properly:"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Continue with ICE PROTECTION FAILURE"
  - kind: comment
    text: "* ICE PROTECTION FAILURE"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Leave icing conditions"
  - kind: line
    number: 1
    text: "Airplane control stick"
    action: "Grasp firmly"
  - kind: line
    number: 2
    text: "AP DISC switch"
    action: "PRESS"
  - kind: line
    number: 3
    text: "Airspeed"
    action: "94 to 152 KIAS (172 KTAS) until final"
  - kind: line
    number: 4
    text: "Flaps"
    action: "UP for landing"
  - kind: line
    number: 5
    text: "Approach speed"
    action: "per table"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Flaps | < 1600 kg | < 1800 kg | > 1800 kg"
  - kind: comment
    text: "UP | 86 | 92 | 96"
  - kind: line
    number: 6
    text: "Landing distance"
    action: "according AFM abnormal flaps"
# The ice shows on both halves of the windscreen; the slow cue gets its own bound (lint L23), an instructor-review value. The icing area ends by itself (the icing exposure of the aircraft physics).
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  message_within_s: 24
  cues[2]: ice_pilot_side,ice_copilot_side
